  "notes": "Base 0-10, teens, and tens per source. 11 పదకొండు, 14 పద్నాలుగు (source exercise), 15 పదిహేను and 19 పందొమ్మిది are attested variants; 12, 13, 16-18 are pattern forms (పది+unit, పన్నెండు/పద్నాలుగు style) not individually source-verified. Compounds 21-99 are two words (tens first, then unit) per source-attested examples. Fractions: naa -nnaara fused forms for x.5 (ఒకటిన్నర = 1.5, రెండన్నర = 2.5, మూడున్నర = 3.5 — last constructed); sagam (సగం, half) is the unmarked word for half and is not included here as it maps to no Hindi fraction key; paavu = quarter, muppaavu = 3/4. Verify with a native speaker. Indian numbering uses lakh/crore; 'వంద' hundred, 'వేలు' thousands (plural, used after numerals)."
